# Copy to .secret (gitignored) and fill in ONE of the blocks below.
#
#   cp .secret.example .secret

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REVIEWERS START HERE. Bring your own key; no Azure resource needed.
#
# Pick a profile and set its key. Either line is a complete setup:
#
#   VISION_PROFILE=openai-gpt-4.1   +  OPENAI_API_KEY
#   VISION_PROFILE=claude-opus      +  ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_FOR_VISION
#
# ⛔ Measured from a cold clone 2026-09-30: without one of these, 9 of the 11
# commands in the README refuse at pre-flight. `log_in` and the tenant refusal
# are the only two that never reach a model.
#
# ⚠️ This file used to offer `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` here, which NO vision profile
# reads -- the field is `anthropic_api_key_for_vision`. Setting the documented
# variable left the run exactly as keyless as before, and said nothing.
VISION_PROFILE=openai-gpt-4.1
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY_FOR_VISION=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Azure profiles (`gpt-4.1`, `gpt-4o`, `gpt-5.2-chat`, `gpt-5.2-codex`) pin
# an endpoint in MY subscription and are unusable without it. Kept as the
# default only because the committed evidence was produced on them.
#   grep '^API_KEY=' ~/workspace/nobsmed-v2/.secret | sed 's/^API_KEY=/VISION_API_KEY=/' >> .secret
# VISION_API_KEY=
# VISION_API_KEY_EASTUS2=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ParaBank demo password. Not a real credential (the app ships with it seeded),
# but it lives here so nothing teaches the codebase that passwords belong in .env.
PARABANK_DEMO_PASSWORD=demo
